diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 9a8a7c9..318a4b2 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -7,3 +7,22 @@ recorded in the audit log. If the sender fails, that notice stays pending.
 The store is in memory so the fixture can be exercised without a database.
 Pending notices are ordered by ID; tenant boundaries are enforced by the
 store. A batch may contain more notices than one page.
+
+## Batch processing
+
+The dispatcher now reads pages so a large tenant does not need one delivery
+loop over the entire pending collection. Page size is deliberately small in
+this example so several pages are easy to exercise. The store returns only
+currently pending notices for the requested tenant, ordered by notice ID.
+After a successful send, that notice is removed from later pending queries.
+
+Batch audit events mark the start and successful completion of a dispatch.
+Per-notice audit entries still follow each successful delivery. A failed
+send is not marked sent.
+
+## Display output
+
+The report module formats a batch count and the sent IDs. Its output is
+intended for operators, not as the source of truth for delivery state.
+The sender now creates a delivery envelope from a notice before forwarding
+the same recipient, subject, and body to the transport.
